course: dictionary
lesson: 5252
title: Join: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word join has several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. Look at the words around it. In «Some children are adopted: they join a family that did not give birth to them», join means to become a member of a family.
explain: In «Hyphens join all the parts of one number», join means to fix parts together so they make one thing. Join can also be a noun: a join is the place where two pieces meet. Ask yourself: are things being fixed together, or is someone becoming part of a group?
explain: Join in and join up are phrases. To join in means to take part in what others are doing. Use the swap check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Join can be a verb (join, joins, joined, joining) or a noun (a join).
fact: To join things means to put or fix them together, like joining two ropes.
fact: To join a group, club or team means to become a member of it.
fact: «A newborn baby has more bones than an adult, because some bones join together as we grow.»
fact: A join is the place where two pieces meet.
exercise: «Hyphens join all the parts of one number.» What does join mean here? | Split apart | Take part in a game | Count them one by one | *Fix parts together so they form one thing
exercise: «Can I join you?» What does join mean here? | To leave a group | To fix two things together | *To come and be with someone | To jump over a fence
exercise: What is a join? | *The place where two pieces meet | A group of children playing | To leave a club early | A kind of rope
test: «A newborn baby has more bones than an adult, because some bones join together as we grow.» Here join together means: | Make a loud noise | *Become joined into one as the child grows | Break into small pieces | Move far apart
test: A friend says, «Let's join forces to finish the project.» What does join forces mean? | Run away from the job | Fight each other | *Work together for a shared goal | Count to ten
exam: «Many puzzles about the body are solved by joining what we know about the body with what we know about energy, heat, light and sound.» Here joining means: | Losing | Breaking | Ignoring | *Combining
